      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6078",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4,$ we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+(z-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+1=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
